  threads on the left pulls into a cone, four gates (Discover, Define,
  Develop, Deliver) narrow it, and an arrow leaves the cone into a finished
  interface. The steps are a real <ol> in reading order; the drawing is
  decoration. Every piece is placed in % of the 600 x 349 box and sized in
  container units, so the whole drawing scales as one; under 600 wide the
  steps leave it for a 2 x 2 grid below.

  THE STRINGS DRAW THEMSELVES (scripts/v4-process.js, _process.css): when the
  drawing comes into view, the four threads are drawn one at a time, in the
  order they end at the right, top first (Vector 12, 10, 11, 13). They are
  inline SVG for that; the rest are images.
#}
